5. Observation time and retrieval time.
6. Spatial/temporal resolution and field-coverage method.
7. Formula/method version.
8. Exact input values and unit conversions.
9. Intermediate steps and assumptions.
10. Confidence/uncertainty and limitations.
11. Related field/crop/alert/action.
12. Links to raw source or report snapshot where permitted.
31. Simple and Advanced modes
Simple: current field, crop/stage, today's weather, water status, urgent risks, next action and readable charts.

Advanced: exact variables, formula breakdowns, raw source metadata, field/grid resolution, soil depths, Kc/Kcb/Ke/Ks, ET₀/ETc, water balance terms, fertilizer nutrient budget, satellite QA, confidence, missing-data policy, model and parameter versions.

Both modes use the same calculations. Switching mode does not trigger recalculation and must preserve selected farm, field, date range and drafts.
PART I — ACCEPTANCE TESTS / RELEASE GATES
32. Data isolation and field switching
- Two farms with different locations never share weather/soil/crop data.
- Two fields with different crop, variety, soil and irrigation show independent results.
- Switching field updates all relevant cards, charts, map layer, alerts, actions and provenance.
- Field selector stays visible and accessible at desktop/tablet/mobile.
- A farm-wide metric remains labelled as farm-wide while viewing a selected field.
- A severe field alert remains visible in farm-wide view even if other fields are healthy.
33. Weather and climate tests
- Forecast, observed, historical and reanalysis values never merge without labels.
- Units and timezone are correct.
- Missing variable or API outage produces partial/unavailable state.
- Forecast rain is not added to observed rainfall ledger.
- Time aggregation does not double-sum interval precipitation.
- Spatial resolution mismatch is disclosed.
- ET₀ formula matches independently verified reference examples and tests.
34. Crop phenology tests
- Crop/variety parameter version is recorded.
- Exact planting date drives the stage model.
- GDD base/upper thresholds and missing-day policy are correct.
- Farmer-confirmed stage is not overwritten by model estimate.
- Calendar fallback is labelled lower confidence.
- No precise maturity date appears when required data is missing.
35. Water and irrigation tests
- ETc = ET₀ × stage-appropriate Kc.
- Dual Kc calculation separates Kcb and Ke.
- Water stress adjusts transpiration using Ks only when the model's inputs exist.
- TAW/RAW use correct soil/root-depth/crop parameters.
- Daily depletion equation balances precipitation, runoff, irrigation, capillary rise, ETc and deep percolation without double counting.
- Depletion is constrained between 0 and TAW.
- Irrigation depth never exceeds modeled refill need unless a separately justified leaching application is used.
- Application efficiency converts net depth to gross depth correctly.
- 1 mm over 1 ha converts to 10 m³.
- Runtime only appears when flow and area are known.
- Pulse count/timing only appears when system and infiltration constraints are known.
- Routine is never counted as actual event.
- Forecast is shown as a projection, not observed water input.
36. Nutrient/fertilizer tests
- Soil-test method/depth/date are retained.
- N, P and K are calculated independently with appropriate calibration.
- Existing fertilizer, manure, residue and irrigation-water nutrient credits are not double-counted.
- Target yield and nutrient uptake assumptions are exposed.
- Product grade conversion and P/P2O5 or K/K2O basis are correct.
- Split timing references crop stage and local recommendation.
- Missing lab/calibration blocks exact-rate prescription.
- Fertigation requires real system capability and safety conditions.
37. Soil and satellite tests
- Lab and mapped estimates remain distinct.
- Soil property depth and uncertainty are shown.
- Texture fractions are checked; invalid sums raise warning.
- NDVI uses actual reflectance bands and QA masks.
- Cloud/no-data pixels are excluded from statistics.
- Coverage and pixel resolution are displayed.
- Low coverage suppresses or qualifies conclusions.
- No NDVI is synthesized from rainfall.
- Satellite vegetation decline never automatically diagnoses disease/nutrient deficiency.
38. Reports, jobs and history tests
- Each report is immutable and reproducible from its input snapshot.
- Source outage creates Partial/Failed, not false Complete.
- Failed run does not replace last successful report.
- Retry is idempotent; no duplicate jobs/alerts.
- Editing a source fact marks only dependent calculations stale.
- Old report keeps prior geometry/profile/crop/model versions.
- User authorization is checked server-side for all farm and field IDs.
39. Release requirement
A feature is production-ready only when UI, data contract, domain calculation, source connection, provenance, persistence, error/partial/offline states, responsive layout, accessibility and automated/manual acceptance tests pass. If a provider, agronomic parameter, calibration or background job is unavailable, mark that feature blocked/planned/unavailable and explain the dependency. Do not simulate a successful connection or calculation.
